 // times per window size (EMA; sizes not seen yet are scaled from seen ones by a prior shape), so the policy adapts
 // to the machine and the context length. It only chooses which drafts to verify: the output is unchanged.
+//
+// T4 (opt-in via set_adapt / --spec-adapt, default off): the MTP window cap itself adapts. Each round the
+// caller deals one cap via mtp_cap() over its min-p cutoff (and T=1 first windows) and passes the dealt size
+// to choose(), which is a pure query: it never deals and never mutates adapt state. mtp_cap() returns the best
+// measured E(t)/cost(t) over that bound, with exploration so the cap can grow back: after 3 consecutive
+// fully-accepted MTP windows at one size the next round probes one size higher (kept when that round also
+// fully accepts); after 2 consecutive zero-accept MTP rounds (size > 1) the anchor drops one immediately; a
+// size untried for ~64 rounds gets one probe (the stalest; ties go to the larger size). Only windows the
+// policy dealt count toward streaks and the stale clock, and every report consumes the outstanding deal (a
+// lookup, a mismatched size, or a duplicate report without a new deal advances nothing); streaks run per
+// dealt size, restarting when it changes. A lookup round breaks the streaks.
